{"reference":"1 Samuel 24","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":24,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"David has an opportunity to kill Saul but refuses to do so. He bases that restraint on Saul's status as the LORD's anointed, even while Saul is pursuing him. The piece of Saul's robe becomes visible proof that David could have acted against Saul but chose not to.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 24:1-22"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_024_40142ec97509254ed397c341"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"In the Larger Story","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"This episode belongs to the larger movement of 1 Samuel: from Eli's failing priestly house, through Samuel's prophetic leadership and Saul's rejected kingship, toward David's anointing, rise, exile, and Saul's death.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_024_28682511258a3f62da3efffd"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}